free-riding is worth 0.489 per round, against the 1 - 2/4 = 0.5 the
marginal per-capita return implies, and the two contribution types earn
the same gross payoff whenever they land in the same group. That gap is
the dilemma: the pot is worth having and nobody wants to pay into it.
